 5. Apple&#x27;s homecoming 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 The Apple HomeView device. Photo: Apple

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Apple today debuted a new device called HomeView — a smart-home product with a 7-inch screen designed to rely largely on voice commands and facial recognition to help users navigate life.

 State of play: The $299 touch-screen smart display device — powered by Siri AI — comes in two versions: one that's mounted to a wall and one that's attached to a stand.

 It can recognize household members by their faces and respond to requests, delivering personalized info, such as calendar appointments. The intrigue: Its debut comes eight years after the release of the Apple HomePod device, which didn't gain much traction .

 Apple unveiled a new version of the HomePod today, the HomePod mini 2, as well as a new version of Apple TV 4K and Apple Home Collection, including smart locks, doorbells and thermostats that work together via the Apple Home app and Siri. 💭 Our thought bubble via Axios' Ina Fried: The smart home has struggled to live up to its early promises, although there are signs consumers may be warming to some categories of devices with modern AI helping make them more useful.

 
 
